{"notes":["info: All three tables (opencode/claude/codex) cover exactly the closed 9-role vocabulary — 9/9 roles, no gaps, no extras.","info: opencode.toml rows byte-match the ratified mapping, including notes (backend light variant alex-backend-light, frontend UI variant alex-frontend-ui, product-review absorbs althea-ux-specialist + althea-review-specialist); all rows mode=delegate.","info: codex.toml is safety-compliant — explicitly states Codex ships native sub-agents today (built-in + .codex/agents/*.toml), frames solo as deliberate pack policy per R4/R8, and defers named-agent delegation to a planning revision. No false capability claim.","info: claude.toml is stock-compatible (every role -\u003e general-purpose, works with zero custom agent files) with the optional named-agent upgrade documented as comments.","info: pack.go embeds mappings/ correctly (//go:embed mappings + fs.Sub, same pattern as skills); RoleVocabulary is the exact ratified closed set of 9 in canonical order; LoadMappingTable refuses unknown ecosystems, unknown/missing roles, unknown modes, mode-inconsistent targets, multi-line fields, and meta/key mismatch deterministically; RenderText emits deterministic plain text with full provenance (version, ecosystem, name, source) in canonical role order — sidecar-suitable.","info: Tests assert the high-value cases: per-table 9/9 coverage, exact opencode rows via DeepEqual (incl. notes), codex all-solo, claude stock default, render determinism + provenance + canonical row order, unknown-ecosystem refusal, and 9 negative validation cases plus a valid-baseline pass.","info: Boundary respected — skills/commands/{README.md,eka-discuss.md,eka-execute.md} in the worktree are identical to the /home/marij/maleolabs/eka/eka-mcp/skills/commands/ baselines (same file set, line-for-line content match); no install/copy/sidecar-writing logic was built, per scope.","info: Dependency hygiene OK — single new direct dependency BurntSushi/toml v1.6.0, go.mod and go.sum consistent (h1 + go.mod hashes present, no stale entries); justified for declarative TOML tables instead of hand-rolled parsing.","info: README.md paragraph accurately describes the embedded mappings/, the closed 9-role vocabulary, delegate/solo semantics, and the future DELEGATION.txt sidecar.","minor: RoleVocabulary is an exported mutable []string — any importer can mutate the shared vocabulary at runtime and corrupt validation/rendering globally. Consider storing it unexported and exposing an accessor that returns a copy (or document it as immutable-by-convention like Capabilities).","minor: No golden-byte test pinning the exact RenderText layout. Current tests prove determinism, provenance presence, and row order, but an accidental format change (column separators, header wording) would pass silently; one small golden-string assertion would lock the sidecar contract.","nitpick: validate() iterates the Roles map for the unknown-role check, so with multiple simultaneous defects the specific error message returned may vary between runs; the refusal itself is always guaranteed.","nitpick: RenderText sizes the header columns with len() but data cells with utf8.RuneCountInString — equivalent today (ASCII header) but inconsistent if the header is ever localized."],"role":"review","verdict":"approve"}